{"id": "tea:vivekamartanda:topic.knowledge-of-own-body", "source": "src:vivekamartanda", "location": {"ref": "topic.knowledge-of-own-body"}, "paraphrase": "How can yogins succeed who do not know in their own body the six centres, the sixteen supports (ādhāra), the three targets (lakṣya) and the five voids (vyoma)?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D). Verse recalled from the Vivekamārtaṇḍa/Gorakṣaśataka family (it opens the Briggs recension's body-mapping); which recension carries it should be checked. The Siddhasiddhāntapaddhati (U21) elaborates nine centres, sixteen supports, three targets, five voids.", "concepts": ["cpt:cakras", "cpt:sixteen-adharas", "cpt:three-laksyas", "cpt:vyoma-pancaka"], "terms": ["trm:adhara", "trm:laksya", "trm:vyoma"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vivekamartanda:topic.mudras", "source": "src:vivekamartanda", "location": {"ref": "topic.mudras"}, "paraphrase": "The seals and locks taught are mahāmudrā, nabhomudrā (= khecarī), uḍḍiyāna, jālandhara and mūlabandha, with viparītakaraṇī to save the nectar from the sun.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "practices": ["prc:mahamudra", "prc:khecari-mudra", "prc:uddiyana-bandha", "prc:jalandhara-bandha", "prc:mula-bandha", "prc:viparitakarani"], "cross_refs": ["tea:goraksasataka:59"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vivekamartanda:topic.six-limbs", "source": "src:vivekamartanda", "location": {"ref": "topic.six-limbs"}, "paraphrase": "Yoga has six limbs: posture, breath-control, withdrawal, concentration, meditation and samādhi (the yamas and niyamas are not counted among the limbs).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "paths": ["pth:goraksasataka-six-limbs"], "cross_refs": ["tea:goraksasataka:4"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
